      "events": [
        {
          "type": "BuiltinCommonInstructions::Comment",
          "color": {
            "b": 51,
            "g": 107,
            "r": 250,
            "textB": 255,
            "textG": 255,
            "textR": 255
          },
          "comment": "The main game includes many different object types and elements:\nSprite objects for the majority of player and enemy objects. \nTiled sprite objects for the backgrounds.\nPanel sprites (9-patch) objects for parts of the UI\nBitmap text objects fro any text.\nA tilemap object for the world layout itself.\n\nThe tilemap was made in LDtk and then imported into Tiled Map Editor, then finally exported into JSON format for use with GDevelop. More about using Tiled Map Editor directly can be found here: http://wiki.compilgames.net/doku.php/gdevelop5/objects/tilemap#creating_a_new_tilemap_step_by_step\nCollisions for the world are handled outside of the tileset, but making a single \"platform\" sprite object then placing as many as needed on the map, then stretching/rotating as required.\n\nAll enemy objects have object variables of enemyDMG and enemyHP for use with combat/damage management in later events.\nThe player has numerous object variables, those are explained in the various events that use them."
        },
        {
          "type": "BuiltinCommonInstructions::Comment",
          "color": {
            "b": 109,
            "g": 230,
            "r": 255,
            "textB": 0,
            "textG": 0,
            "textR": 0
          },
          "comment": "The main event sheet for the level only contains events that must be included at the start of the scene."
        },
        {
